+1. Delivery address is lost: POST /api/orders accepts address in body but createOrder ignores it — orders table has no address column. Fix: (a) create db/migrations/002_add_order_address.sql with: ALTER TABLE orders ADD COLUMN address TEXT; (b) in controllers/orderController.js createOrder: destructure address from req.body; if fulfillment === 'delivery' and no address provided, return 400 { error: 'Delivery address is required' }; include address in the INSERT (add column + $6 param). Check db/migrate.js first to match the migration file convention.
+
+2. Orders on CLOSED shops: createOrder verifies the shop exists but never checks is_open. Fix: after fetching the shop, if shop.is_open === false, return 400 { error: 'Shop is currently closed' }.
+
+After edits, run npm test and fix any test failures. Then list every file you changed.

