# 2026-09-27 16:14:22.402424
+ONE-SHOT MODE: one turn, apply edits with your edit tool now, no narration. Fix API route mismatches in apps/partner against the real backend (routes/deliveryRoutes.js, routes/kycRoutes.js — READ them first).
+
+Backend truth:
+- GET /api/delivery/requests (list; singular 'delivery')
+- PATCH /api/delivery/requests/:id body {status} — transitions: requested->accepted->picked->delivered
+- POST /api/kyc (submit), GET /api/kyc (my status). There is NO /kyc/status and NO earnings endpoint; delivery_requests has no payout column.
+
+Fixes in apps/partner/src/api.js:
+1. fetchKycStatus: GET '/kyc/status' -> GET '/kyc'
+2. fetchDeliveryRequests: GET '/deliveries/requests' -> GET '/delivery/requests'
+3. acceptDelivery(id): POST '/deliveries//accept' -> PATCH '/delivery/requests/' with body { status: 'accepted' }
+4. updateDeliveryStatus(id, status): PATCH '/deliveries//status' -> PATCH '/delivery/requests/' with body { status }
+5. fetchEarnings: DELETE it. Earnings summary must be computed client-side in Dashboard.jsx as count of requests with status 'delivered' — label it 'Deliveries completed'. NEVER invent rupee amounts; backend has no payout model.
+6. verifyAuth: send { idToken, role: 'partner' } (explicit role, like seller/mart apps).
+
+Fixes in apps/partner/src/App.jsx:
+7. Protected(): hard role block — if firebaseUser is logged in but role is neither 'partner' nor 'admin', render an access-denied screen ('This app is for delivery partners') with a sign-out button, instead of redirecting into partner routes.
+
+Then update Dashboard.jsx if it used the old api function signatures. Run npm run build inside apps/partner until it compiles cleanly. End with the list of files changed.

